Spoilers ahead: how to know for certain if it's safe to eat


DaveH:
 >1) the game has to tell you that you're full.

Marty:
 It does not.  "Sated" to me means not hungry at all, not full to the
 point of vomiting and choking on it.  And how often does anyone do
 that anyway?  The Romans has Vomitoriums, I doubt they'd do that if
 they collected dead bodies.

Listen.  nethack is _not_ the real world, Ok?  It doesn't _have_ to
follow the laws of physics or human common sense.  How many times does
this need to be said.

If you see the word "Satiated" on the bottom line, that means you
shouldn't eat anymore.  If you do eat more, you run the risk of choking
on your food.  Ok?  Is that enough of a hint.

DON'T EAT WHEN YOU SEE THE WORD SATIATED ON THE SCREEN.

If you don't see "Satiated" on the screen, you can eat anything and you
won't choke.

Marty:
 Maybe the message needs to be spit out into "sated" and "gorged".

Oh come on.  How much hand-holding do you need?  Besides, there's no
need to change the message.  Now you know for certain that eating when
it says "Satiated" is dangerous.

I'll say it one more time DON'T EAT WHEN YOU SEE THE WORD "SATIATED" ON
THE SCREEN.  You might choke on your food and DIE.

